# wannado-wce Cursor Co-Pilot Rule

For complete 5-stage workflow instructions, read `.agents/skills/wannado-wce/SKILL.md` (or `AGENTS.md`) and run `wannado-wce inspect .` first.

0. **Scope & Coexistence (`wannado-drl` / `wannado-adv`)**: Activate `wannado-wce` ONLY for wireless environment modeling, 3GPP/ITU parameter provenance, JIT simulator selection, and physical consistency auditing (`./wce_lab/`). Hand off RL training to `./drl_lab/` and RF robustness testing to `./adv_eval/`.
1. **Inspect & Compose (`inspect` -> `compose` -> `diff-spec`)**: Run `wannado-wce inspect .` if needed, compose directly with `wannado-wce compose "<goal>"` (asking 1–2 questions only when ambiguous), and track parameter tweaks via `wannado-wce diff-spec`.
2. **Isolated `./wce_lab/` + Verified JIT Glue (`jit-recipe --verify`)**: Use `wannado-wce scaffold --query "..."` (exposing `ComposedWirelessEnv`), `wannado-wce eject <block_id>`, and `wannado-wce jit-recipe <tool_id> --verify` (reporting `synthetic_contract_smoke` vs `live_runtime_probe`).
3. **Link-Level PHY & 10-Check Gate (`wannado-wce verify`)**: Run `wannado-wce verify --dir ./wce_lab --seeds 0 1 2`, `preflight_wce()`, and `evaluate_link_level_phy()` when coded OFDM/MIMO BLER/EVM is needed.
4. **Traceable Table I & Verbatim Citations**: Run `evaluate_wce_suite(..., run_audit=True)` + `report.save("./wce_lab/outputs")`, delivering `environment_provenance.md` (System Parameter Table I + charts), `paper_params_table.tex`, and zero-hallucination `references.bib` (`wannado-wce cite`).
